      "year": 2022,
      "shift": "25 Jul 2022, Shift 1",
      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "The molar conductivity of a $0.01\text{ M}$ weak monobasic acid is $19.0\text{ S cm}^2\text{ mol}^{-1}$ and its molar conductivity at infinite dilution is $380\text{ S cm}^2\text{ mol}^{-1}$. The dissociation constant ($K_a$) of the acid is $x \\times 10^{-6}\text{ mol L}^{-1}$. The value of $x$ is _______. (Nearest Integer)",
      "image": null,
      "answer": {
        "min": 25.0,
        "max": 25.0
      },
      "solution": "Degree of dissociation $\\alpha = \\frac{\\Lambda_m}{\\Lambda_m^0} = \\frac{19}{380} = 0.05$.\n$K_a = C\\alpha^2 = 0.01 \\times (0.05)^2 = 10^{-2} \\times 2.5 \\times 10^{-3} = 2.5 \\times 10^{-5} = 25 \\times 10^{-6}$.\nTherefore, $x = 25$."
    }
